    "problem_statement": "# Issues with pickling files in different modes and states\n\nI'm having problems with pickling files in certain modes and states. The behavior seems to have changed recently.\n\n## Reproduction\n\nHere's a simple script that demonstrates the issue:\n\n```python\nimport cloudpickle\nimport pickle\nimport tempfile\nimport os\n\n# Create a test file\nteststring = \"Hello, world!\"\nwith tempfile.NamedTemporaryFile(delete=False) as tmp:\n    tmpfilepath = tmp.name\n    tmp.write(teststring.encode('utf-8'))\n\n# Try to pickle a file in read mode\nwith open(tmpfilepath, 'r') as f:\n    try:\n        # This used to work but now fails\n        pickled = cloudpickle.dumps(f)\n        unpickled = pickle.loads(pickled)\n        print(f\"Read mode content: {unpickled.read()}\")\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"Error with read mode: {e}\")\n\n# Try with a file that has a specific position\nwith open(tmpfilepath, 'r') as f:\n    f.seek(4)  # Move to position 4\n    try:\n        # This used to preserve the position but now resets to 0\n        pickled = cloudpickle.dumps(f)\n        unpickled = pickle.loads(pickled)\n        print(f\"Position after unpickling: {unpickled.tell()}\")\n        print(f\"Content from position: {unpickled.read()}\")\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"Error with seek: {e}\")\n\n# Try with a closed file\nwith open(tmpfilepath, 'w') as f:\n    f.write(\"test\")\n# f is now closed\ntry:\n    cloudpickle.dumps(f)\nexcept Exception as e:\n    print(f\"Error with closed file: {e}\")\n\n# Clean up\nos.unlink(tmpfilepath)\n```\n\n## Issues\n\n1. Files in read mode ('r') can no longer be pickled\n2. File position (seek position) is not preserved when pickling\n3. The logic for checking if a file is closed seems inverted\n4. Files in read+write mode ('+') no longer work correctly\n\nThis seems to have broken backward compatibility with previous versions."
